<title>SWEDEN: FORECAST-Atlas Copco higher profit '96.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Atlas Copco higher profit '96.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish industrial engineer Atlas Copco was expected to post a seven percent higher profit after financial items of 3.03 billion crowns in 1996 against 2.84 billion crowns in 1995, a Reuters poll showed on Monday.</p>
<p>Forecasts from 14 analysts varied between 2.81 and 3.21 billion crowns.</p>
<p>The analysts forecast Atlas Copco's profit would continue to rise, reaching 3.24 billion crowns in 1997 and 3.63 billion crowns in 1998.</p>
<p>The company's board was expected to increase its 1996 dividend payment to 3.45 crowns a share compared with 3.00 crowns in 1995.</p>
<p>Analysts interviewed for the poll were from Aros, Deutsche Morgan Grenfell, Enskilda, Fiba, Fischer, Handelsbanken, James Capel, Kleinwort Benson, Matteus, Morgan Stanley, Paribas, Penser, Swedbank, and Ohman.</p>
<p>Atlas Copco will publish its 1996 figures on February 13.</p>
<p>PROFIT AFTER FIN (MLN SKR)</p>
<p>				   AVG	 RANGE	  ANALYSTS</p>
<p> 1996			   3,028     2,810-3,213	  14</p>
<p> 1997			   3,244     2,770-3,650	  13</p>
<p> 1998			   3,632     3,300-4,000	  12</p>
